An existing directory path with `[id]` is taken literally, not as a glob character class, so the glob view lists `[id]/page.md` but not `i/other.md`.
== args
input/app/[id]
== file input/app/[id]/page.md
---
description: Product detail page.
---
# Page
== file input/app/i/other.md
---
description: Must not match the [id] character class.
---
# other
== stdout
glob view: input/app/[id]
input/app/[id]/page.md (4 lines): description: "Product detail page."
== stderr
== exit 0
